          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.467,
            0.846,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": "？ What property do you think this digital root will have? Recall that we did this while finding the divisibility shortcut for 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.517,
            0.847,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** If a number is divided by 9 then the digital root of the dividend is the remainder. If the number is exactly divisible by 9 then its digital root will be 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.58,
            0.845,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": "Between the numbers 600 and 700, which numbers have the digital root: (i) 5, (ii) 7, (iii) 3?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.628,
            0.205,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.645,
            0.847,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": "(i) Digital root 5, from 600 to 700 are (Sum of digits are 5(1 + 4 or 2 + 3)) 608, 617, 626, 635, 644, 653, 662, 671, 680, 689, 698."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.687,
            0.846,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Digital root 7, Sum of digits are 7, 16 (0 + 7, 1 + 6) 601, 610, 619, 628, 637, 646, 655, 664, 673, 682, 691"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.73,
            0.845,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Digital root 3, sum of digits (3 means 12, 21) 606, 615, 624, 633, 642, 651, 660, 669, 678, 687, 696"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.776,
            0.846,
            0.817
          ],
          "content": "？ Now, find the digital roots of some consecutive multiples of (i) 3, (ii) 4, and (iii) 6."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.824,
            0.205,
            0.842
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Ans."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.847,
            0.574,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": "(i) Digital roots → 3, 6, 9; 3, 6, 9; ......"
        },
